tags: network-bytes-per-day

A limit of the node: the most bytes that the node relays through ServiceTunnel in one day, for all the clients together.

The value is an integer in bytes. Example: 107374182400. The day is the calendar day of the node, in its local time zone. When the node has no bytes left, it refuses the traffic with RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=network-bytes-per-day
per=all the clients of the node together
rule=The day starts at 00:00:00 of the local time of the node: the time of the concept 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:76016d6a59ad50c6aed0620ea7d772e9f3ec634a40cac7a94785b23768dae900 plus the offset of the time zone that the host of the node uses. When the node has no bytes left, it refuses the traffic with the status RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED (the number 8) of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:601d79f95bb7809d28f01f0a66f82f77d00ed850faa1b02627b0ac7a6f398345.
scope=none
unit=bytes
